Report a reset stream's final size on the event that announces it.

RFC 9000 4.5 settles a stream's final size when RESET_STREAM arrives,
and draft-ietf-webtrans-http3-16 5.4 requires it to implement
WT_MAX_DATA: without it the two endpoints disagree about how much
session credit a reset stream consumed. MsQuic already holds the value
as Stream->RecvMaxLength, documented there as the immutable final size,
but PEER_SEND_ABORTED carries only an error code and the statistics
struct has no byte counts, so an application cannot read it.

The value is added to the event rather than exposed as a stream
parameter. An application learns the final size exactly when it is
settled, in the callback that tells it the stream was reset, and does
not have to call back into the API from inside that callback to ask.
It also needs no new parameter identifier: MsQuic allocates those
sequentially with no reserved vendor range, so any value an
out-of-tree caller picks is one upstream may later take.

UINT64_MAX means the final size is not settled, which is the value
RecvMaxLength already carries until a FIN or RESET_STREAM sets it.

diff --git a/src/inc/msquic.h b/src/inc/msquic.h
--- a/src/inc/msquic.h
+++ b/src/inc/msquic.h
@@ -1663,6 +1663,11 @@ typedef struct QUIC_STREAM_EVENT {
         } SEND_COMPLETE;
         struct {
             QUIC_UINT62 ErrorCode;
+            //
+            // The final size of the stream, settled by the RESET_STREAM frame
+            // (RFC 9000 4.5). UINT64_MAX if it is not yet known.
+            //
+            uint64_t FinalSize;
         } PEER_SEND_ABORTED;
         struct {
             QUIC_UINT62 ErrorCode;
diff --git a/src/core/stream_recv.c b/src/core/stream_recv.c
--- a/src/core/stream_recv.c
+++ b/src/core/stream_recv.c
@@ -174,6 +174,7 @@ QuicStreamIndicatePeerSendAbortedEvent(
     QUIC_STREAM_EVENT Event;
     Event.Type = QUIC_STREAM_EVENT_PEER_SEND_ABORTED;
     Event.PEER_SEND_ABORTED.ErrorCode = ErrorCode;
+    Event.PEER_SEND_ABORTED.FinalSize = Stream->RecvMaxLength;
     QuicTraceLogStreamVerbose(
         IndicatePeerSendAbort,
         Stream,
